      "correct_answer": "B",
      "explanation": "Tinea unguium (onychomycosis): most common nail infection. Subungual hyperkeratosis, distal/lateral onycholysis. Most common organism: T. rubrum. Treatment: terbinafine (oral, 6-12 weeks)."
